5.25 Hz lies between the 0.5-Hz FFT bins. Its energy therefore spreads across neighbouring frequency bins instead of appearing as one sharp line. That is the spectral leakage the lab asks you to explain.

Frequency resolution is \(\Delta f=f_s/N=1/T\), so increasing the observation time improves frequency resolution. Spectral leakage occurs when the observation interval does not contain an integer number of cycles of a sinusoid, causing discontinuity between the beginning and end of the sampled record. Its energy then spreads into neighbouring FFT bins.
