As the sampling rate decreases, fewer samples represent each signal cycle and the waveform becomes increasingly discrete. With \(f_s=15\) Hz, the 10 Hz input exceeds the Nyquist frequency of 7.5 Hz and therefore aliases to 5 Hz. A sampling rate of approximately 100 Hz gives 10 samples per cycle and visually represents the 10 Hz waveform much more clearly.

